<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-UPP half-yr profit up 88.9 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE-UPP half-yr profit up 88.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    1.72   vs     0.91</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   1.49   vs     0.79</p>
<p>    Turnover			     27.38   vs    33.02</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  0.65   vs     0.97</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation   2.49   vs     2.98</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			2.66   vs     1.63</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.94   vs     0.72</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		     0.19   vs     0.22</p>
<p>Note - United Pulp &amp; Paper (UPP), a timber company, said it expects the group to remain profitable in the second half. It said its better performance in the first half was largely due to continuing increases in management efficiency, strengthening of the US dollar against the Singapore dollar and a reduction in interest expenses.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
